  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community-to-Society Impact Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bahia Street (Bahia Street), $252,153 over 4 years Bahia Street will continue to offer additional educational opportunities through a program of tutoring and mentoring for 75 girls and at-risk youth (6-17 years) in Salvador da Bahia, Brazil, in elementary school so they can have access to secondary and higher education. In addition to the 75 girls and young women benefited from the core curriculum, new programmatic activities offered on an experimental reach about 200 additional beneficiaries, involving a wider range of community stakeholders, such as parents, guardians and teachers to strengthen the development of the students of Bahia Street.</narrative>
  </description>
